WEBVTT

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.130
Daimon Shugo.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:21.310
He's made eight appearances in the summer and spring Koshien tournaments.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.400
Out of those eight, he's won it all once, and gone to the semis twice.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:30.260
He's coached four teams and has gotten good results for all of them thus far.

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:33.370
On paper, he's a top-notch coach that any team would welcome.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.270
But despite all of his accomplishments,

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.450
not a single player from the four teams he coached has ever really made it big.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.830
A few of them did crack the professional leagues,

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.960
but they've all quit from the stress built up since their high school days.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:52.900
He doesn't really seem like the type who would give a damn about his players' futures.

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.750
Now that you mention it,

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:58.770
didn't he resign once because his school got banned from playing?

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.250
That was the year after he won the Koshien.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:04.780
He basically abandoned the team because they lost a lot of talent that year.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.010
He actually encouraged his third-years to do some bullying,

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:12.560
then secretly reported it to the High School Baseball Association himself.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.460
Whoa.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.820
Would he really go that far?

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.930
You'd hope not.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:28.150
But those baseball transfer students must've heard those same rumors before coming here.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.600
I'm surprised they came.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:34.570
Guys with talent always think they're the exception.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:40.980
Plus there's no denying that this <i>is</i> a fast track to the Koshien.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:48.550
So, what do you want to do, Akaishi?

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:51.450
You wanna play under that coach?

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.670
No way.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:53.760
Let's kick him out, then.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.100
Do you have a minute?

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.930
Coach Daimon?

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:58.590
What can the middle school team do for you?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.120
I'm just taking a look.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:03.420
I want to see if there's anyone I can use next year.

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.860
Please, take a seat.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.290
Center field!

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.030
Shortstop!

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.420
Quite an impressive bunch, I must say.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.880
Well, they're...

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.590
Who's that pitcher?

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.310
That's Tsukishima, a ninth-grader.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.720
She's the captain.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:39.050
She's got quite an arm on her, doesn't she?

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:42.260
Everyone's impressed when they first see her.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.600
A girl?

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:49.540
Yes, but she really loves baseball, that one.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.810
I didn't come here to look for baseball fans.

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.330
Would you like anything to drink?

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.310
I'm fine.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:58.110
Thanks for your time.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.500
Center field!

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.080
I got it!

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.000
Come on, old man!

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.870
Each team has its own environment and circumstances.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.470
There's more than one way to practice, you know.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.230
Would you wake up and talk sense for once?

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:25.120
The first-stringers are calling you the "has-been coach" in case you didn't know.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.070
It's all about being creative with what you have.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.940
Right field!

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.180
A bunt?

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:37.730
Hurry it up!

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:41.620
Such a pleasant sound.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.030
<i>Tsukishima Wakaba...</i>

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:57.300
<i>You were right about him.</i>

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:12.930
Keep going.

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.640
Yes, sir!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.350
He'll burn out.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:23.640
That's fine.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:26.400
That's the reason he's here in the first place.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.130
Want to bat?

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:31.100
I'd rather take practice swings than hit a pitch like that.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:34.590
For you, I could let Kamikawa pitch.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.590
He'd just lose his confidence.

00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:38.540
Or would you rather have our ace pitcher...

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:40.980
break down as well?

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.350
No, that'd do us no good.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.620
I'm heading out to the pitching machines, then.

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:52.720
Wait, there is someone.

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:58.300
Someone you could practice with and who we wouldn't mind burning out.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:16.090
Thank you!

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:20.550
You're late.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:22.310
I'm sorry.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:26.120
My elbow felt a little strange, so I had the school nurse take a look at it.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:28.890
She said it was pretty badly swollen

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.250
and that I should sit out practice for today.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.560
She also said that I shouldn't pitch for the time being.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.130
Here's my doctor's note.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:37.570
I see.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.340
Then you're no longer useful to the first-string team.

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:45.700
Pack your things and report to the Prefab farm.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.230
Well, I'm pretty sure the nurse was just exaggerating.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.440
I'll pitch, don't worry.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:53.220
I'm totally fine.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.720
I'll go get changed.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.580
T-Tsukishima?

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.190
All right, let's get started.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:06.890
Yes, sir!

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:20.180
Thank you for waiting, Miss.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.120
Here you go.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:23.420
Keep the change.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:25.850
Thank you, as always.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:30.310
But are you sure it's okay for you to skip out like this when you're the manager?

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:33.150
Is anyone <i>complaining</i> about it?

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.770
I guess you have a point there.

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:38.770
It won't be my turn until this team becomes famous,

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:41.650
and the press starts rolling in and out of here.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:44.330
Now that you mention it,

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.420
I was just walking past the baseball team just now,

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.740
and I saw Tsukishima Aoba pitching.

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:50.320
Tsukishima Aoba?

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:51.730
Oh yeah.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.640
I guess you wouldn't know since you were abroad, Miss.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:58.030
She's really famous among the middle schoolers.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:00.670
She's cute and she's good at sports,

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:02.960
plus she's popular with both the guys and the girls!

00:09:02.960 --> 00:09:06.380
She throws a really good fastball on top of that.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:09.850
Oh yeah, the coach did mention someone like that yesterday.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:13.710
He said she'd make the perfect disposable batting practice pitcher or something.

00:09:16.190 --> 00:09:19.100
Come on, isn't there too much ice in this thing?

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.820
Can you please elaborate on what you mean?

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:27.110
There's too much ice, duh!

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:28.940
I meant what you said before that.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:30.110
Who the hell are you?

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:35.150
We're the terrifying Prefab team!

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.170
Round two.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.020
Hurry up and pitch already!

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.290
What's taking you so long?

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:07.570
Who are <i>you</i> guys?

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:10.350
It's them, Coach!

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.820
Those are the three from the Prefab team who didn't take the selection test.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.560
I see.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.230
They look as if they're confident in their baseball skills.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:23.850
Damn, he saw right through us.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.470
I guess he's not a top coach for nothing.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:31.430
I don't know what you're up to,
but you'd do well not to cross me.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:34.610
Or I'll have you spending the next three years on the dung heap.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:36.390
The dung heap?

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:40.050
The Prefab team is a "farm" team by name only.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:42.730
I have no intention of harvesting any talent from it.

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:47.160
In other words, you Prefabbers are nothing but fertilizer for the first-string team.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:50.530
That's a harsh way to put it.

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:55.100
How much longer are you going to make her pitch?

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:57.890
Until she faints.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:00.010
It doesn't matter if she's injured or breaks down.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:03.250
She's a talent that we can't use in official games, after all.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:06.630
However, she makes for an excellent fertilizer.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:14.150
Your speed's not too shabby, but you're still a girl in the end.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:15.990
They're flying off my bat like it's nothing.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:38.530
You better watch out.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:43.980
You may just trip onto the dung heap yourself,
wearing sunglasses as dark as those.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:56.660
Why, that...

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:00.530
It's my turn, isn't it?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:42.330
Looks like your motor's finally warmed up.

00:12:42.330 --> 00:12:46.610
I never thought I'd <i>want</i> to face a girl pitcher.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.550
What an honor.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:53.100
You better set your engine to full throttle.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.490
Get me a different catcher, then.

00:12:55.860 --> 00:12:57.120
Hey!

00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:58.930
You saying I'm not good enough?

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.500
Sorry.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:01.920
I'm a sucker for looks.

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:02.760
What?

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.200
Akaishi.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:07.750
Go get 'em, stud.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.200
She's calling for you.

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:11.410
What should I do?

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:13.540
Go.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:20.310
Dammit! "A sucker for looks" my ass!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.280
Okay, I'm all set.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:28.690
A Prefabber, huh.

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:31.730
I'm part of the <i>baseball team</i>, just like you.

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:42.480
No way!

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.410
That's way faster than before.

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:55.350
Azuma missed?

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:01.290
It's not every day you see her pitching at full strength.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:08.160
She only gets to pitch in practice games. But if she threw her
hardest, it wouldn't be very good practice for the batters.

00:14:10.670 --> 00:14:12.440
Strike two.

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:13.780
You're against the wall now.

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:15.040
What next?

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.530
I'll just have to...

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.910
I'll just hang on with fouls.

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:37.190
Look, none of them are flying forward.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:44.610
They're all going straight back.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.110
Yeah.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.200
He's getting the timing right on every pitch.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:54.220
If he actually managed to get even half the ball with that swing...

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.340
It'd fly out of the park.

00:15:05.320 --> 00:15:06.580
You punk.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:09.420
I haven't had such good practice in a while.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:20.830
Could someone wipe this down?

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:22.330
Yes, right away!

00:15:24.930 --> 00:15:25.950
Please, sit down.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:29.690
Listen carefully, you two!

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:33.110
This is Shido Risa, the first-strings' manager.

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:37.490
She's our acting principal's daughter who's actually lived abroad.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:40.170
At school overseas, she was really popular,

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.180
and was even voted their Miss Transfer Student...

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:43.990
Are you two even listening?

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.470
What a silly girl.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:54.930
What's the point in getting all muddy and exhausted?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:57.450
How pathetic.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:02.770
But she's way hotter than a girl who only has her looks and her dad to brag about.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:04.620
Right, Kitamura?

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:07.180
Cut it out, Senda!

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:09.700
She's going to hear you if you say it so loud like that.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:15.050
No, it wasn't me, I swear!

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.410
Good evening, this is Adachi Mitsuru.

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.930
That's not even close!

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:25.090
I guess no one beats Ko when it comes to impersonations.

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:26.750
Yeah.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:30.530
He's always been good at mimicking other people's voices.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:32.810
Like the one he used to do of the grocer, right?

00:16:32.810 --> 00:16:33.910
Nah.

00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:37.060
His best has definitely got to be the one of Gen from Uomasa.

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:39.190
Yeah, there's no topping that one.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:52.460
Quit yawning, you bimbo!

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:54.500
Right, Kitamura?

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:57.630
N-No, that wasn't me I swear!

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.440
Do you want to throw for her?

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:07.270
Yeah.

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:09.980
I'd love to pummel him with a pitch.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:12.780
I guess that makes three of us.

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:17.940
Where do you think you're setting up?

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:25.540
She's more of a man than you.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:29.330
Yeah. More than you, too... Way more.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:25.420
Why don't we wrap it up here for today, Coach?

00:18:26.760 --> 00:18:31.960
It'd be a shame if this top-notch batting center
broke down on us after just one day.

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:33.660
You're right.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.980
All right, everyone to fielding practice!

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:37.040
Yes, sir!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.460
That girl's in the way.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:40.110
Get her off the field!

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:41.910
I've become pretty patient, haven't I?

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:45.240
If this were middle school,
I would've jumped that guy by now.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.170
Yeah.

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.350
Third base!

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.060
Yes, sir!

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:53.300
One more!

00:18:53.300 --> 00:18:54.150
Yes, sir!

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:56.890
Next, outfield!

00:18:56.890 --> 00:18:57.630
Yes, sir!

00:18:57.630 --> 00:18:59.210
Right field!

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:00.190
Yes, sir!

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:21.690
Why are you sitting next to me?

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:22.870
Are you freaking serious?

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.650
I wouldn't have done it if Akaishi hadn't asked me to, you know.

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:27.240
I can carry my own bag, thank you.

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.530
Ow...

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:34.720
Don't listen to what that sunglasses punk tells you to do ever again, okay?

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:37.720
Or you'll really end up breaking down.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:39.290
Not on my watch!

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:41.930
I know you're upset, but you can't beat Azuma.

00:19:41.930 --> 00:19:43.160
Just give it up.

00:19:44.960 --> 00:19:47.250
Isn't it your job to do that?

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.650
If they let me pitch just one more time,

00:19:54.650 --> 00:19:58.810
I can at least find out all the <i>other</i> batters' weaknesses.

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.370
What are you...

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:06.500
I don't have any faith in you!

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.040
Not one little bit!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.050
What the hell?

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:13.410
It's just...

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:15.480
Mifujidai, Mifujidai.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:32.640
So, you were saying?

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:43.160
I just want to be able to believe in what Akaishi and Waka told me.

00:20:43.160 --> 00:20:44.460
What Wakaba said?

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:45.520
What was it?

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:50.170
She said once he becomes serious, he could be Japan's best...

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:51.900
Japan's best?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:56.470
<i>Once he gets serious,</i>

00:20:56.470 --> 00:20:59.220
<i>he could become the best pitcher in Japan!</i>

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:02.010
<i>He might even be able to throw 160km/h.</i>

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:05.630
<i>My predictions tend to come true, you know.</i>

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:20.920
Japan's best what?

00:21:23.870 --> 00:21:24.620
Come on!

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:26.860
What's with that sigh?

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:30.500
Come on, tell me!

00:21:33.090 --> 00:21:35.130
Damn it!

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.630
So you don't like to lose, huh.

00:23:13.630 --> 00:23:14.570
You guys are alike.

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:16.140
Who are you talking about?

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:17.970
I get it.

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.280
So you're nervous about your debut game, huh?

00:23:20.280 --> 00:23:21.650
Yeah, right.

00:23:21.650 --> 00:23:26.120
Treat me to the Napolitan over at Clover cafe if I manage to hold the first-string team to ten runs.

00:23:26.120 --> 00:23:28.440
It's got to be cooked by Ichiyo, of course.

00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:29.850
Make it five runs.

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:31.120
Cheapskate.

00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:33.920
Next time, on Cross Game Episode Eight:

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:35.560
You Guys are Alike.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:37.220
Who are you calling a cheapskate?
